senses.gloss:
varavarṇin, a. having a fair complexion;
 -inī, f. fair-faced woman. [varavarṇa,
1230.]

várṇa, m.
 —1. outside; external appearance;
 color, 36^19, 37^6, etc.; complexion;
 —2. (color, and so, as in Eng.) kind,
species, sort, 98^2;
 —3. (sort of men, i. e.)
caste, 28^18;
 —4. letter; sound; vowel,
59^16; syllable; word, 98^3. [√1vṛ, ‘cover,’
1177a: for mg 1, cf. Eng. coating, and
coat (of paint), and Lat. color, prop.
‘cover or coating,’ cognate w. oc-cul-ere,
‘cover over.’]

vártra, a. warding off, holding back;
as n. a water-stop, dam, weir. [√1vṛ,
‘cover,’ q. v.]

1várdhana, a.
 —1. increasing, trans.;
as m. increaser;
 —2. delighting in.
[√1vṛdh, ‘increase,’ q. v.]

várman, n. énvelope; coat of armor;
protection; at end of Kshatriya-names,
59^13N. [√1vṛ, ‘envélop,’ 1168. 1a.]
